          "quote": "(comp (ref \"U15\") (value \"SN74LVC1G07QDCKTQ1\") ... (field (name \"MPN\") \"U74LVC1G125G-AL5-R\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"U22\") (value \"SN74LVC1G07QDCKTQ1\") ... (field (name \"MPN\") \"U74LVC1G125G-AL5-R\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"U35\") (value \"SN74LVC1G07QDCKTQ1\") ... (field (name \"MPN\") \"U74LVC1G125G-AL5-R\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"U36\") (value \"SN74LVC1G07QDCKTQ1\") ... (field (name \"MPN\") \"U74LVC1G125G-AL5-R\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "single non-inverting buffers (SN74LVC1G07, parts U15, U22, U35, U36) wired as /OE-controlled sinks"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "If the MPN is used for sourcing or assembly, the e-stop sink outputs will be push-pull rather than open-drain. This can change sink-line behavior and may actively drive a line high where the intended circuit expects a sink or high-impedance state.",
      "confidence": 0.84
    },
    {
      "category": "bridged_nets",
      "components": ["U21", "U20"],
      "pins": ["U21.13", "U21.15", "U21.3", "U20.2"],
      "nets": ["+3V3"],
      "observed": "The FT231XS 3V3OUT pin (U21.13) is tied to +3V3, which also connects the external regulator output U20.2; the FTDI VCC and VCCIO pins are on that same rail.",
      "expected": "An internal regulator output should not be tied to an independently regulated board rail unless the FTDI datasheet explicitly permits that configuration. Use the FTDI 3V3OUT only as specified, or leave it separate when externally powering the device at 3.3 V.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"+3V3\") ... (node (ref \"U20\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"VO\")) (node (ref \"U21\") (pin \"13\") (pinfunction \"3V3OUT\")) (node (ref \"U21\") (pin \"15\") (pinfunction \"VCC\")) (node (ref \"U21\") (pin \"3\") (pinfunction \"VCCIO\")))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The FTDI internal regulator output may contend with the board's 3.3 V regulator or be back-driven, potentially causing excess current, unstable supply behavior, or damage.",
      "confidence": 0.77
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The files show a sourcing/part-identity conflict in the e-stop buffer path: the specified open-drain parts have push-pull 1G125 MPNs. They also connect the FTDI 3V3OUT pin to the externally regulated +3V3 rail, creating a likely regulator-output conflict."
}

